X-Deja-AN: 145129533
organization: University Communications, Inc.
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec

This may be a stupid question, but we haven't figured out the answer yet.

We're trying to use raw disk partitions, and are finding that writing to
the block device (e.g. re9e) is MUCH slower than writing to the character
device (rre9e). Now, I could understand that if they were unaligned access,
but if that's the answer, I've been unable to find the right alignment.
Specifically, I've used 320*7*64 bytes (8*35 512-byte sectors), I'm simply
opening the raw device r/w, and writing without doing any seeks. The 8*512
factor in there should handle any power of 2 block sizing up to 4K.

If I use the character device, I can get about 3800 sectors written
per second; I get less than 1/10th that doing it to the block device.
