Jason new wrote:
> 
> I need to get a performance comparison between an old
> VAXstation 4000 model 90a (which has a VMS specmark
> of 39) and a new Alphastation 200 4/100 or 4/166.
> 
> All of the specs I have seen for the 200 are running unix
> and using SpecInt etc, but I know of no way to directly
> compare the two measurements. I spoke to DEC here,
> but they couldn't help me on this one.... is there anyone
> out there who can??
> 

All the Alpha systems are faster than the 39 SPECmark VAX. 
The SPEC89 rating is based on on 10 benchmarks (4 int+ 6 fp).
Since most RISC systems have higher FP ratings than int ratings,
the SPECint to  SPEC89 comparison will only understate the performance
advantage of the RISC machine.
If you have the individual SPEC ratios for the 89 suite, you can 
calculate SPECint89 for a fairer comparison to SPECint92.

