In article <4ji134$9th$1@mhadg.production.compuserve.com>, kd <74146.3703@CompuServe.COM> writes...
>Is there a way to do disk partitioning under RSTS V9.3 (or any 
>version for that matter)?  I have a client who installed a new 
>hard disk, and RSTS is telling him that it is too big when he 
>tries to DSKINT it or to MOUNT it.  Is there any way to make RSTS 
>think that it is actually 2 smaller disks?
> 
>Thanks!

What sort of controller is the drive on?  Most 3rd-party MSCP-emulating
drive controllers allow you to do the partitioning in the firmware's
controller.  Some (i.e. CMD SCSI controllers, Emulex SMD controllers) allow 
you to partition each physical
drive into two logical drives, while others (i.e. my Webster ESDI controllers)
will allow each physical drive to be partitioned into as many as 8 logical
drives.

