Tel: (310) 820 7365		E-mail: info@4front-tech.com
Fax: (310) 826 2465		Web: http://www.4front-tech.com
_____________________________________________________________________________

4Front Technologies announces UNIX Sound System (TM)

4Front Technologies is announcing the availability of UNIX Sound System
(USS) - a universal audio architecture to support digital audio and MIDI 
on UNIX workstations. USS is based on the popular Linux sound driver 
architecture.

UNIX Sound System is a set of device drivers that provide a uniform API 
across all the major UNIX architectures. It supports "Sound Blaster" 
compatible sound cards which can be plugged into any UNIX workstation 
supporting the ISA, EISA or Microchannel bus architecture. USS also 
supports workstations with on-board digital audio hardware.

Traditionally, each UNIX vendor has provided their own API for processing 
digital audio. This meant that applications written to a particular UNIX 
audio API had to be re-written or ported, with possible loss of 
functionality,  to another version of UNIX. Applications written to the USS
API, need to be designed once and then simply re-compiled on any supported 
UNIX architecture. USS is "source code" compatible across all the platforms.

Most UNIX workstations, thus far, have only provided support for digital 
audio sampling and playback (business audio). USS brings the world of MIDI 
and electronic music to the workstation environment. With the advent of 
streaming audio, speech recognition/generation, computer telephony, Java 
and other multimedia technologies, applications on UNIX can now provide 
the same audio capabilities as those found on Windows NT, OS/2, Windows 95 
and the Macintosh operating systems. USS also provides synchronized audio 
capabilities required for desktop video and animation playback.

Functionally, USS provides support for:
---------------------------------------
o 8bit and 16bit stereo digital audio playback and sampling (up to 48 KHz)
o FM sound synthesis
o MIDI input and output
o Audio Mixer for setting input and output levels
o Wavetable synthesis for MIDI playback

The UNIX architectures supported by USS are:
--------------------------------------------
o IBM AIX 4.1 on PowerPC, RS/6000 (beta)
o Linux on Intel x86 (beta)
o SCO Open Desktop on Intel x86 (beta)
o UnixWare on Intel x86 (beta)
o FreeBSD and NetBSD on Intel x86 (beta)
o Solaris on Intel x86, PowerPC (3Q96)
o SunOS and Solaris for the Sparc (3Q96)
o BSD 4.4 on Intel x86 (3Q96) 
o Digital Unix on DEC Alpha (3Q96)
o HP-UX on HP PA-RISC (3Q96)
o SGI-IRIX on MIPS (4Q96)

The sound cards supported by USS are:
-------------------------------------
o Creative Labs (Sound Blaster)
o Gravis (Gravis Ultrasound)
o Media Vision (Pro Audio Spectrum)
o Microsoft Sound System
o MediaTrix AudioTrix
o Ensoniq Soundscape
o Turtle Beach sound cards
o Analog Devices' PSS chipset based sound cards
o Oak Technology's Mozart Sound based sound cards
o OPTi chipset based sound cards (MAD16 & 930)
o ESS Technologies chipset based sound cards (ESS1688 & ESS688)
o Crystal Semiconductors chipset based sound cards (CS4231 & CS4232)
o Audioware/6000 MCA sound card (ESS1688)

The on-board audio supported by USS are:
----------------------------------------
o PowerPC with CS4231 chipset
o PowerPC with CS 4232 chipset
o Intel x86 with ESS, Creative Labs, etc. chipsets
o Sparc with CS4231 chipset (planned)
o Sparc with AD 18xx chipset (planned)
o PA-RISC with CS 4231 chipset (planned)

USS is an "Open Systems" compliant API. The API programming
documentation
will be available from 4Front's WWW site. Most public domain
applications
written for Linux will be able to compile without modification to the
audio
sections.

