Oh dear.  I don't think that would ever work.  UTP stands for unshielded
twisted pair, and there is a twisted pair for both send and receive, i.e.
4 separate wires.  How any passive component such as a balun could mix
these signals onto a single coax cable, I don't see.

Perhaps you're thinking of some slower-than-Ethernet IBM terminal wiring
scheme that happens also to use RJ45?  These are not UTP Ethernet devices.

