In article <826299121.12188@steves.scg.co.uk> steves@scg.co.uk (Steve Smith) writes:
>I'm porting some software from Unix to VMS and need to open the stdin
>device in a mode so that echo is switched off and each character
>can be got without waiting for a CR/LF.

Using functions from the curses library:

1.  Call noecho to turn off the echo.
2.  Call crmode to allow single characters to be snarfed.
3.  Call getch to snarf a character.

$ HELP CC Run function
$ HELP CC/VAXC Run function
	-or hopefully-
$ HELP CC/DECC Run function

describes each function.  However, crmode (at least) is referred to as
``[no]crmode''.

Also, if you're using VAX C (compiler version 3.2 or lower), you'll have to
explicitly link against the curses library.  See the documentation for details.
				/AHM
