Couple of quick things you could check

1. have someone power the drive on while you watch the front lights. They 
should all flash once if not you may have a burnt out bulb and may just 
not be seeing the error code.

2. change the cabling from port A to port B and on the KDB or whatever 
try to change ports as well.

These drive were historically sensitive to belt tension and heat.

3. check to see if the belt is white on the inside.If it is ..change it.

4. make sure the fan behind the motor is running freely and is 
unobstructed.


Good luck

Brian V






