Still kinda different. The problem with the PC array is inter-box latency,
and the expense of doing the connects (via switched HIPPI).

DEC is _claiming_ app->app 1-byte latency of 4-usec. I dunno if SGI has the
HIPPI number under 200 by now (originally around 2 _ms_...; 200 usec is
probably around theoretical min...). Coupled with the fact that it's
easy to set up multiple memory channels among multiple DECs, the 
DEC config should be a _big_ win over the SGI for anything with any
latency sensitivity (like the bulk of message-passing codes, and all
software parallelized 'serial' codes...).

DEC's got a new connect arch; SGI's still shipping old technology
(both are outdated bus-based SMP arch's...).


