In article <1996Mar25.105224@cjis.ci.lincoln.ne.us>, tech@cjis.ci.lincoln.ne.us (Tim Travis/City of Lincoln/Data Processing) writes:
>        I have a cybernetics 8mm tape drive attached to a differential 
>        SCSI cmd controller card CQD243. I would like to put Digital drives
>        on this controller, probably RZ28s. Has anyone had ecperience with
>        doing this?

If the CMD controller has only a single bus, then don't.  It's definitely not
advisable to mix disk and tape on the same SCSI bus.

I have put RZ28 drives (and DSP3210 drives) on a different CMD controller, the
CMD Hawk (CI-SCSI) and have had no problems.  In fact, they worked far better
than Seagate drives which gave us some grief initially (we ended up not
accepting the Seagate drives and purchasing all Digital drives, and haven't
tried any Seagates since, although I have heard that the problems have since
been fixed).

