The LK451 is an LK411 with LK450 legends.  It was created because
the LK450 keyboard could no longer be sold in Europe due to some
stricter regulations that came into effect this past January 1st.

>  2.   Is it possible to use a LK411 keyboard together
>       with Windows NT and an Alpha based DEC workstation

Yes, I think this should work.  It's just a matter of finding the
right driver.  Even without the driver, all the "common" keys between
a PC layout keyboard (PCXAL) and a VT layout keyboard (LK4XX) should
work just fine (i.e., F11-F20, KPminus, Compose may not work).

