Hi all,

Couple of days ago I put a message on this news group wondering about
the errors I am getting from the comiler.  I am getting a lot of 
Floating exceptions. So I thought that my code is not compatible with
the new gcc (2.7.2) that I just upgraded to. This code has been working
fine for 2 years on ALL other platforms. But Mr. Mardahl suggested that
it could be:

1) assigning invalid data (uninitialized memory) to a variable (even if we
   never used the variable again and didn't care about he value)
or
2) doing a division by zero (which SunOS would just ignore)

but after extensive testing I have come to the conclusion that there
is something wrong with the OS or gcc. 
This is what I got from the gcc news group:

In ref. to my recent posting (it has expired on or server, so I
cannnot do a followup on it), Tim Mooney gave the following
reply (and caught that it was not an error, but a warning. I
called DEC up and got the patch and it fixed that problem. It
was interesting to look at the README that came with the patch
to see all of the other problems it fixed.
THANKS Tim!
Cheers,
Douglas

This was the article:

When compiling gcc-2.7.2 and g++, I get the following error in
several places (or one similar to it):

No, you get the following *warning* in several places -- we've seen it on
our alphas too.  The information I've heard is that it's a relatively minor
problem with DEC's ld (or possibly `as', I forget which but I think it was ld),
and the warnings can safely be ignored.  However, if you have a support
contract with Digital you can get patch OSF350-086.  It's fixes about 30
seperate problems with `ld', including:

PROBLEM:        (Patch ID: OSF350-086)           (QAR 30052)
********
ld outputs erroneous warning messages about exception info when linking
modules with no text region.

>/usr/bin/ld:
>Warning: Linking some objects which contain exception information sections
>   and some which do not. This may cause fatal runtime exception handling
>   problems (last obj encountered without exceptions was version.o).

Tim


*******
Could anyone tell me where I can get this patches for my DEC (other that
the DEC support group, we have left a message with them a while ago and 
we have not heard anything back yet!!!).

Thank you in Advance,
Sincerely,
Nader Behzad
