I've compiled and am using both fvwm 1.24r and fvwm 2.0.41 on Digital UNIX
3.0 and 3.2c - I used the DEC compiler 'cause gcc tends to give me more
problems.  Previous versions of fvwm 2 (then called patch levels) were a bit
buggy and annoying but 2.0.41 is quite nice with no (that I have found) bad
bugs (a couple of minor quibbles with the way it parses commands though) so
I'm using it as my default window manager.  It's a bit bigger and slower
than fvwm 1.24r but still smaller and faster than mwm.

