acmecsp@ix.netcom.com(Donald E. Dayton ) wrote:
>I have two power supplies labeld "LA120 Power Supply" still wrapped in
>anti static.  They don't look anything like the H7150-D's that are in
>the LA120's I have now.
>Can anyone give me some information on these and if/how I can use them?
>The number on side two of these new boards are 5013043D-5413044.
>Thanks
>S.K.
>ACMECSP@IX.NETCOM.COM

There were 2 different power supplies used in the LA120.  The original 
one used a largish transformer, a bridge rectifier, some LARGE capacitors 
and a regulator module (traditional power supply).  What you may have is 
the regulator module (I don't remember the part number, but 54-13044 
sounds right).

The newer LA120's used a switching power supply (the H7150).  It didn't 
need the big transformer and caps so it was cheaper to build, and being a 
switching supply, it was more efficient than the old bulk supply.

