In article <4iume8$q81@news.indy.net> ACS@Indy.net (Strider) writes:

>Could someone please tell me what a system 1032 is? is this hardware or 
>software? is it still being used much?

System 1032 is the VMS version of a database management system originally
designed for the DECsystem-10 (and later DECSYSTEM-20) called System 1022.
The company that created it was Software House (later bought by CompuServe
and re-named CompuServe Data Services, or something like that; they have
now bought themselves back, and are called Praxis), of Cambridge, Mass.

There are still System 1032 BOFs at DECUS, so *somebody* must be using it
enough to care.

We still have customers running applications based on System 1022.
