>man page on digital unix implies that this is also the case for digital 
>unix. However, on 2 separate systems, I get 0.

See also: hostid, the part about also being able to set the host id.

Alpha systems do not have a system unique hardware identification
number.  Good thing too, since many people hate the licensing hassles
of having to get a new license to move their software between systems
when one is broken.  If you want to the hostid to be a unique number
use hostid when the system boots to set one.

If you still insist upon licensing around unique hardware numbers
you consider the Ethernet address of the built-in Ethernet adapter.
This is a unique number.
