In article <4j83e2$966@eclair3.cs.cornell.edu>, soam@cs.cornell.edu (Soam Acharya) writes:

>I've cloned the OS distribution (Ultrix 4.3 ) off an internal disk of a
>DECstation 5000/20 to an external SCSI disk: it's a 2 Gig Conner CFP1080S.
>I'm pretty sure I'm installing the boot block on the disks but I cannot get
>the Dec to boot off the external disk.  There are no problems in mounting
>and reading the disk though.

The ULTRIX kernel knows what its system is.  It is the part of the
kernel configuration file that goes:

config vmunix root on ...

Just cloning an existing system isn't going to change.  If you didn't
rebuild the kernel to know the name of the system disk this is most
likely the problem.  I am taking a wild guess at this since you've
offered no clues as to what the problem really is.

>
>I notice that in the FAQ it says that releases of Ultrix 4.2A and before
>wouldn't work with SCSI disks larger than 1 GByte.  Could this be a 
>problem? 

If the FAQ says pre-V4.2A, then it is wrong.  It should be pre-V4.2.  The
V4.0 and V4.1 SCSI drivers were limited to addressing 1 GB of disk capacity.  References outside that range would wrap around.  Disks larger would still
work as long as you were willing to give up the extra capacity.  Since you're
running V4.3 this isn't the problem.

