Well, seems I was misinformed about the Micro/PDP-11 I just collected!
It is actually an 11/23+, rather than an 11/03 as previously
suggested. This is, all in all, good news, since it means I may have
some chance of running something interesting on it ...

The machine (was part of an X-ray crystallography rig) had not been
run for 5 years. I lugged it home on the back seat of my VW beetle and
plugged it in. to my suprise, RT11 booted ...

The next few hours were spent stripping the machine down and cleaning
thoroughly. Having been in a lab, the system was pretty
filthy. Naturally, when I reassembled it, it no longer booted. After
several hours of trying every trick I could remember, I replaced all
the disk cables, and the cable from the controller to the distribution
panel, with spares from my junk box. Suddenly it all sprang back into
live ... phew ... I'd hate to break it after all these years. Moral -
beware dodgy/marginal cables and connectors folks.

So, I have an 11/23+, in a floor-standing box. Inside:

	M8189	11/23+ CPU
	M8087	RAM board (half populated, 128Kword)
	M7857	Serial multiplexer (4 lines)
	M8043	Serial 4 SLU unit (NO LONGER INSTALLED)
	M7941	Parallel line unit (NO LONGER INSTALLED)
	M8639	RDRX controller

There is also an RD51 (10Mb) winchester and an RX50 dual
floppy. Interestingly, the parallel board had been hacked to control
some experiment or another.

Questions: 
---------

1) What is the difference between the 4 SLU board and the serial MUX?
I take it that the MUX uses only one CSR/VEC and the 4 SLU board uses
multiple addresses?

2) The RD51 seems pretty slow, and the access LED on the drive glows
faintly when there is no access, and brighter when there is. Is the
failure of the LED to turn off completely normal, or is it a sign of
poor cabling?

3) I have a 1Mb memory board from a MicroVAX II. Can I use it in the
11/23+? I guess not, since the uVAX uses a private memory interconnect
scheme, absent in the -11. We can all dream.

4) How do I format RX50 diskettes on a PC? I gather there is some
program to do so ... the -11 (Digital being Digital) can't do this for
itself.

5) I need an operating system. I have RT11, RSX-11M and UNIX (v6,v7)
on my 11/34a. Unfortunately the 11/34a uses RX01s and RK05s, for which
I have no QBUS controller. I'd ideally like to move v7 to the
11/23. Failing that, a copy of RT11 on RX50s would be very nice, since
the installed RT11 is a bit of a mess, and I'd like to start
afresh. Any OS needs to be able to support the RD51 (and ideally the
RX50). Suggestions?

6) Errm ... that's it.

Cheers,
Bob.
