In article <1996Mar19.100959@axp2.umkc.edu>, randrew@axp2.umkc.edu
(Andy Rupf) writes:
:An alpha workstation is giving me the error
:%system-w-ProxyConvert old format needs to be converted
:or roughly that.  So I need to update or convert my proxy database.
:Anyone know how to do this?

  The details of using the CONVERT_PROXY tool are listed in the OpenVMS
  V6.1 installation manual.  I'd recommend reading the manual, but here's
  the quick version:

	You need DECnet running.

	$ SET SERVER SECURITY/EXIT
	$! alter the following if NET*PROXY files are not in SYS$SYSTEM:
	$ DEFINE NETPROXY SYS$SYSTEM:NETPROXY.DAT
	$ DEFINE NET$PROXY SYS$SYSTEM:NET$PROXY.DAT
	$ RUN SYS$SYSTEM:CONVERT_PROXY
	$ SET SERVER SECURITY/START

  Do *not* delete the old NETPROXY database, and make sure that -- if
  it is not left in the default SYS$SYSTEM: location -- that the necessary
  system-wide NETPROXY logical name (still) tracks its location.

  Again, reading the manual is recommended.

  Given the lack of configuration and version details, I'll mention that
  you may/will also want to review the System Management manual and the
  VMScluster manual around maintaining common files in a VMScluster.
  And that you will want to manage the proxy database from a V6.1 or
  later OpenVMS VAX system, or from an OpenVMS Alpha V6.2 or later
  system, whenever one of these versions is present in a VMScluster.

  ------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
