>
>----- CAM STRING -----
>ROUTINE NAME                            cdisk_complete 
>----- CAM STRING -----
>                                        Retries Exhausted 
>----- CAM STRING -----
>ERROR TYPE                              Hard Error Detected 

I think these tell you about as much as anything; there was an error,
the driver tried very hard to retry the command, but the it kept
failing.  Since there isn't any sense data, it suggests that the
disk isn't responding at all.  If you can, see if the disk is
even spinning.

The power cycle to get it back sounds like power is getting lost
somewhere, but it is interrmittent.  It could even be the disk
is running too hard and decides to shut itself off.  That would
probably happen more often though.

>
>Any hints appreciated.

Looks like a broken disk.  Whether it is power, electonics, termites...;
can't tell, since the disk doesn't say.
