Nader Behzad (nbehzad@ee.ualberta.ca) wrote:

: I get floating exception problems when my source is compiled with gcc2.7.2.
: This code has been working on every other platform (using gcc2.6.0).

The Alphas are pretty unique in their behavior that they will issue
a FPE on loading a float or double from memory that doesn't contain a
valid floating point number (usually unitialized data).  Most systems
don't give the FPE until you actually try to compute something with it.

I.e.

	double f = x;			<-- FPE's here on the ALPHA
	f = f / 2;			<-- FPE's here on the Sun.

-Ron



