Well I have a uVAX II which uses a PC as a terminal. Here's what I
did ...

The console port is the nine pin connector on the LED panel at the
back. I used a 9 to 25 way adaptor, a 25 pin "modem" cable, and a
gender changer (not a null modem) to connect to a 25 pin IBM PC style
RS232 port.

The 4 25 way ports are DZ11 additional serial ports. To connect to
these you need to have VMS or somesuch running and recognising the
ports. The 25 way modem cable, plus a null modem will do here. Note
the use of the null modem for the DZ11 ports, but not for the console.

Hope this helps ...

Bob
