|
|      I have a couple of CDC SMD drives I would like to put on my 
|   uVAX II. I have a System Industries controller board. Could 
|   someone tell me:

|	 1. What bus priority this board has

No idea.

|	 2. What is the proper method for daisy chaining these drives

There should be three cables on the SMD controller. A thick ribbon and
a pair of thinner ribbons. The thick ribbon connects to the
appropriate connector on the drives, daisy-chaining the pair of drives
together. One thin cable goes to the corresponding connector on each
drive - doesn't matter which goes to which drive. Get the connectors
the right way up, or it won't work! 

Drive ID is selected by throwing DIP switches on the drives
themselves. One drive should be zero, the other one. 

(Only) The last drive on the bus should be terminated - this is
usually effected by putting in resistor packs (that look like ICs) in
the sockets next to the "thick cable" connector. The other drive (not
at the end of the bus) should have no termination.

|	 3. What is the drive name under VMS

DUA0:, DUA1: etc.

Cheers,
Bob
