>because it has the terminators soldered in and I boot the machine.  It
>sees the drive as "DKA200", but if I try to INITIALIZE or MOUNT the disk
>I get a an error stating that I can't (I think "fatal hardware" or 
>something error).  When I do a "SHOW DEV DKA200" it say's that it is
>a "generic SCSI" disk and won't tell me the size.
