I thing your problem is the same one I had.  I tried to install a Quantum 
Fireball on a VAXstation 3100 under VMS 6.0 and got the same Fatal 
Hardware message.  The problem is that VMS before version 6.1 could not 
handle the long messages sent back by some drives in response to the 
inquire command.  I believe there is a patch for older versions of VMS.  
I just loaded VMS 6.1 and the problem went away.  The Fireball has worked 
fine since.  Also the termination on the Fireball is selected by jumper, 
not by removing a set of restore packs. This same Fatal Hardware messages 
also occurred with a 1 GB IBM disk.


                                     Peter Lang
