references: <4ijc7q$1ff@news.rrz.uni-koeln.de> <4il30r$2ei@rainbow.isds.duke.edu> <4iloob$og@news.rrz.uni-koeln.de>
organization: Institute of Statistics and Decision Sciences, Duke University
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec

In article <4iloob$og@news.rrz.uni-koeln.de>,
Markus Dickebohm <acp66@rrz.Uni-Koeln.DE> wrote:
>
>Astonishing.  I did not get ctwm to work neither fvwm2. They are both
>available for the DEC-platform at our regional computing center but
>when I put them into my ".xsession"-File they don't start and I get
>the error message:
>	"sbin/loader: fatal error"
>The only way to start them is to kill "mwm" and start the new WM by
>hand. Unfortunately the any mouse operation does not work like
>expected. Especially fvwm2 has a strange behaviour:

It sounds like something in your environment is misconfigured.  The 
message you're getting may mean that these window managers depend on
shared libraries that can only be found by your interactive
environment; not by the environement that's present when executing
your .xsession script.

I'd suggest trying one of the following:

a) making your .xsession file run in an environment that's identical
to the environment you use for interactive sessions.  Ie, if your
.xsession is a sh script & you normally run csh, change it to be a csh
script & make sure that csh scripts have access to the same paths &
environment variable used in interactive sessions.

b) grabbing ctwm & compiling your own copy.  Link this statically.

Drew
