Hi Eugene,

when ESDI was popular I used to set up many VMS systems with ESDI system 
disks. In fact I've got one running at home. With newer controllers you 
shouldn't have to bother about drive geometry. EMULEX as well as DILOG 
(and I suppose all other vendors) added an option to read the geometry 
from the drive, where it is stored in a local NVRAM. This worked fine, 
whenever I tried it.

If your controller doesn't have this option I might be able to help you 
as well. I have parameter lists for various drives in the office. Just 
send me an e-mail, specifying which drive and controller models you are 
using. Maybe I can dig something up.

Regards,
Dietmar




