If your disk was connected on a PC, try a low level format.
Every Vaxstation has a low level format routine (i hope so).
I found the following instructions in the "VAXstation 3100
Model 38  Owner�s Manual".



>>> TEST 75	<Return>

ScsHDerase
PV_SCS_FMT_CHN	(0=SCSIA, 1,=SCSIB)?	0	<Return>
PV_SCS_FMT_ID	(0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7)?	2	<Return>
PV_SCS_FMT_RUSURE	(1/0)?		1	<Return>

PV_SCS_FMTING ..........................
PV_SCS_FMT_BBrepl=0				(Number of bad blocks is listed)

PV_SCS_FMT_SUCC

>>>


I hope this procedure will work.


Good luck,




