I am running DEC OSF/1 V3.0 Worksystem Software (Rev. 347)
with  DEC OSF/1 V1.3 Worksystem Software [Rev. 111] .

In using (Digital) grep on files with very long records (over
700 fields per record, fixed record length) grep truncated
silently returning only about half the number of fields.
This caused a substantial problem in a computation that
did not explicitly check on the number of returned fields.

Is this a well known problem with (Digital) grep? Has anyone
else encountered it? I have reproduced the problem on another
DEC ALPHA running Digital Unix.

Gnu grep does not seem to have this problem.
May be I should be going Linux all the way if DEC can't get it 
straight?

