Alphas using the 21066 chip do NOT run VMS.   Examples include the
AXPpci33 "NoName" motherboard (EBP20-xx & EBP22-xx) and, I believe,
the Multia.   I am told that the reason centers around the software
differences in the way the chip communicates with the external world
(I/O bus, etc.).

The AXPpci33 is available with Digital Unix and Windows/NT, but it
is incapable of running VMS.   I wish that this were not true, and
expressed my disappointment at the DECUS symposium in San Francisco.
The response from the VMS developers was that they decided "there
wasn't enough of a business reason to do so".

