>not pretty, but it worked.
>
>-- 
>Christopher M. Conway		wombat@aquilagroup.com
>
>Don't Tread on Me

If you had bothered to pick up and read an RTL manual you would have saved
yourself a lot of frustration. The library routine to create a sub-process
is LIB$SPAWN. To do it from DCL the command is SPAWN. The /NOWAIT or
/DETACH qualifiers are used to get the two processes to run asynchrously.

Most environment information is inherited by the new process. Logical names
created with the /JOB qualifier are shared between parent and child process
via a common logical name table.

You can also create processes via Decnet - 
  ie. nodename"userid password"::TASK=command-procedure.

You can also RUN SYS$SYSTEM:LOGINOUT.EXE/lots-of-qualifiers.

You can also use the system service $CREPRC.

SHEESH!!! Did you really have trouble with this?

