In article <4hupql$n8p@caesar.ultra.net>, delrios@ma.ultranet.com (John Del Rios) writes:
> Went through several setups and configurations of Buslogic hardware and=20
> firmware with and without help from Buslogic tech support. They are stumped=
> ..
> 
> Before I trash the board & Buslogic...any suggestions. Thanks for the help.

  Let me guess - you just disconnected the drives from the onboard con-
troller and connected them to the BusLogic and expected them to work,
right?

  Different SCSI controllers report different geometries for the same disk
drives. MS-DOS (and MS-DOS derived systems, like Windows) have an unfor-
tunate dependency on disk drive geometry (the first partition is expected
to start on cylinder 0, head 1, sector 1).

  You'll need to back up your disks, do a clean install with the BusLogic
in place, and then restore from the backups. If you have a spare drive,
you could run it on the BusLogic while leaving the other drives on the
onboard controller and just copy your files over. You need to make sure
that the disk on the BusLogic was freshly formatted (the BusLogic should
have a menu option to do this) so that any trace of the incorrect geometry
configuration is wiped off the disk before you start.

