Have a look at Scotty at the following URLs:

http://www.cs.tu-bs.de/ibr/projects/nm/scotty/welcome.html
ftp://ftp.ibr.cs.tu-bs.de/pub/local/tkined
I think there is a ftp mirror somewhere in the USA.

Scotty is an extension of Tcl/Tk scripting languages. So, you'll have
to get them too. All that is free software. I know it runs on UNIX
systems. For other systems, check what the scotty F.A.Q. says. It is
able to do exactly what you mentioned in your example. Tkined is a GUI
which can be used with scotty scripts but you can also run them in the
background without a controlling terminal.

After having compiled all that, you'll have to play with it for a
while to get the idea how it works. Unfortunately, the documentation
is rather poor due to, as far as I know, the fact that the package is
written by university people in Germany, i.e. it is made by a
non-profit organisation.

