  In the US: 1-800-DIGITAL: EK-VT220-RM (refman), -TM (techman), -UG
  (owners guide), -HR (pocket guide).

  Terminals after the VT220 are largely upward compatible, so a manual
  for a later VT-series terminal is generally a superset of the VT220.

  And if you want just a list of the escape and control sequences and
  have an OpenVMS system handy, look in the file sys$system:smgterms.txt
  -- this and the SMG documentation should be enough to deal with the
  commonly-used escape and control sequences.

  And if you have an OpenVMS system, SMG allows you to dynamically "look
  up" the escape and control sequences for either a Digital-supported or
  a site-specific terminal under full program control.

