The problem is solved by using "nslookup" from bind-4.9.3 instead of the one 
on Ultrix.  Here comes the summary:

=============================================================================
From: scheib@olympia.mcis.washington.edu (Jeff Scheib)

All 23 DEC 5000/2??'s running ULTRIX V4.4 (Rev. 69) do NOT have a problem with
"nslookup" distributed with OS.  Our /etc/svc.conf looks like:
aliases=local,bind
auth=local
group=local,bind
hosts=local,bind
netgroup=local
networks=local,bind
passwd=local
protocols=local
rpc=local
services=local

=============================================================================
From: "S.Grant" <grant@psc.edu>

If you've recently upgraded your nameservers/resolvers to the new
release of bind, nslookup supplied by Ultrix cannot communicate with
them.  Build a new one for Ultrix 4.4 or use dig.

-Shirl

=============================================================================
From: grosen@dilbert.cc.ndsu.nodak.edu (Johannes Grosen)

This is probably due to the incorrect behavior of nslookup on the
ultrix box. It uses an old, deprecated method of querying a nameserver
which newer releases of bind refuse (4.9.3). I believe that if you
were to replace the `nslookup' on the ultrix host with the one from
the recent bind distribution you would find that things work fine.
