: : root?  

First, see if you have any junk lying around in your root partition,
i.e., core files, old log files, old copies of the kernel.  You might
just want to do a find and look at any file over a given size.

Second, you don't allocate additional space to root, you move stuff
off of the root partition.  For example, and probably not a good
example, if root is on rz0a, you could might move everything in /etc
to rz0d and then mount rz0d at /etc.  We've gotten in the habit of
mounting all our partitions at the top level and then using links to
where they should go, i.e., we have a /mail with a link a
/var/spool/mail. Moving all this stuff around is a pain, which is why
I like the Advfs with dUnix since then I can allocate additional space
without disturbing my users.

--

