>disk drive as dka400:

This is most likely your problem, the ROMS in the 3100 don't know about
anything bigger than a 1Gb disk.  If you try to make a >1Gb disk your 
system disk you should expect all sorts of troubles (as you are seeing).
VMS, once it's running, doesn't have any problems with bigger disks than 
that.  Ditto for standalone backup.  Probably your best bet is to shoehorn
VMS onto one of the rz23s.  You might do this by installing it on the
2.9 Gb external, then removing all of the extraneous parts (for hardware 
and CPU that don't match your system), then doing a backup/image of the
result to the smaller disk.  Alternatively, scrounge up a <1Gb (formatted)
SCSI disk for your system disk (probably your best bet). 

One other point - nonDigital system disks won't boot from a power up on a
3100.  During the power up sequence the ROMs apparently check to see if the
system disk is marked Digital (don't ask me how) and then bails before it
gets to the "boot".  If you enter boot at the >>> it will then boot
normally.  It will also reboot from a shutdown - just not from a cold
start. 

>
>When I try to install VMS on the external disk drive and try to boot
>off of it during the install:
>
>boot dka500
>
ok

>loads the standalone backup
>
ok

>then I do
>
>backup/image/verify dka500:vms061.b/save_set dka400:
>

That will work because standalone backup can handle >1Gb disks.

>it installs it fine and then when you have to reboot to continue the
>install process, it gives the following error on the console screen:
>
