You only terminate the devices on the ends of the bus (usually the
controller and the last device in the daisy chain).  

If the "power" pin to the resistor packs comes from either a diode
or a fuse then a diode, it is probably passive termination and
the component is a 220/330 resistor network.  Another way to
check is if the pin opposite the power pin is attached to ground,
which you can check with an ohmmeter to the case or the center
two pins of the power connector.

If the "power" pin comes from a voltage regulator (it has 3 pins in
case you didn't know that), or a fuse then a voltage regulator,
then it is probably active termination and requires a 110 ohm
resistor network with one side common.

-Gary




