>:a user's _FTAnn: process will start consuming huge amounts of CPU.
>:
>:SHOW PROCESS/CONT reveals the priority is flashing around a lot, up to 16!
>:What the heck is a user process (running at base priority 4) doing with
>:priority boosted to 16?  
>
>   It sounds like its related to rundown processing -- it could be a
>   quota-related.  Process priorities also get bumped when a mutex is
>   being held.
>
>:Anyway, so far it has only happened on IBMs running AIX.  The Phase X
>:terminals, Suns, and Alpha consoles have been clean.  It could just be
