>
>   You'll probably want to crash the system, and submit a problem report
>   to Digital with a copy of the dump file.  (These problems can be a bear
>   to try to diagnose in this forum -- particularly when one does not have
>   access to the dump file.)
>  
>  ------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
>   Stephen Hoffman      OpenVMS Engineering      hoffman@xdelta.enet.dec.com
>  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
>

I've seen a similar problem on both VAXes and Alphas.  We were using
our own terminal driver and what would happen is the user would delete
the window instead of logging out normally.  The driver noticed that
the window wasn't there and tried to write an error message.  It
couldn't do this because the window wasn't there.  So,  it tried to
write an error message...  The result a process that chewed up the CPU
and really wasn't accomplishing anything.  In our case we could fix
the driver.  I realize that this isn't the same problem but,  you
might try deleting the window and see if that reproduces your problem.


