In article <4h7j8f$qqp@bigboote.WPI.EDU>, bad@wpi.edu (Bernard Armin Doehner) writes:
>
>Could someone please tell me how I can configure my DS3100 so that
>I get text-only on my console rather than the default X-Windows
>(Xprompter)?

Edit /etc/ttys so that rather than "on" the X server line is "off".
At the same time, change the /dev/console line so that it is "on"
rather than "off".  Verify that you've done both of these things
and then type "kill -HUP 1".  You will have a very dumb console,
but an interesting amount of memory back.

>How can I change the resolution that is used on the console?

The color and monochrome frame buffers are limited to 75 dpi.
