mathog@seqaxp.bio.caltech.edu wrote:
>One other point - nonDigital system disks won't boot from a power up on a
>3100.  During the power up sequence the ROMs apparently check to see if the
>system disk is marked Digital (don't ask me how) and then bails before it
>gets to the "boot".  If you enter boot at the >>> it will then boot
>normally.  It will also reboot from a shutdown - just not from a cold
>start. 

When I looked at this, it appeared that the problem was not non-DEC 
disks, but disks whose SCSI INQUIRY ID was longer than the ROMs had 
allowed for.  (I think 7 or 8 characters)

For example, a Micropolis 1588 works fine (including cold boots). If I 
remember correctly, it's ID is 1588-15.

A Seagate ST431200N (a Wren VII) will not cold boot.  I don't remember 
the ID, but it's something like 11 characters long.

FWIW: The Wren VII will boot fine with a VAXstation 4000-VLC.  
Interestingly enough, a SHOW DEVICE has the SCSI ID truncated.  It 
appears that they fixed the ROMs, sorta.

