Christophe,

I never received your email message, but in any event, here it goes.

> We have 6 IPC with these damn DECchip 21040 / PCI and Digital doens't
> provide a simple packet driver for DOS so we can use it ?

The Digital network product business unit does not have a packet driver for
our DC21X4-based adapters (DE434, DE435, DE450, DE500).  Since there are
numerous companies that buy and use the DC21X4 chips, you may be able to
find a packet driver from someone outside of Digital.

For clarity, the network product business unit is separate from the
semiconductor group that developed, sells, and supports the DC21X4
family of chips.  That's why you'll find device drivers from the network
product business unit that are *different* than what's available in
generic DC21X4 driver kits.  This is intentional.  You can think of
Digital in the same light as National Semiconductor in this respect.
We sell networking chips on the open market, but we also have a
separate division that productizes plug-in hardware using some of
those chips.

If at all possible, please use the DOS NDIS 2.01 or DOS ODI drivers
with your networking software.  We (network product business) do have
a packet driver in the development plans, but no promises on delivery.
Hope this clears things up.  Please keep in mind that Digital is a large
(over 60K employees) corporation, with various business units.
